  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Dilip Kumar Giri vs The State Of Bihar on 21 November, 2022 Author: Prabhat Kumar Singh Bench: Prabhat Kumar Singh In The High Court Of Judicature At Patna Criminal Miscellaneous No.28893 of 2022 Arising Out of Ps. Case No.-637 Year-2021 Thana- Motihari Town Distr Champaran ====================================================== 1. Dilip Kumar Giri S/O Bal Yogeshwari Giri R/O Village- Karamwa Madhopur, P.S.- Gamhariya, District- East Champaran 2. Bal Yogeshwar Giri S/O Indrasan Giri R/O Village- Karamwa Madhopur, P.S.- Gamhariya, District- East Champaran ... ... Versus The State Of Bihar ... ... Opposite Party/s = = = = = ======================================== = Appearance : For the Petitioner/s : Mr. Jitendra Kumar Giri, Advocate For the Opposite Party/s : Mr. Umeshanand Pandit, App",
    "facts": "As per prosecution case, 25-26 trainee constables, after taking meal in mess, of which these petitioners are in charge, became ill and started vomiting and felling ill, dizziness and pain in abdomen.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel appearing for the petitioners submits that petitioners are innocent and have falsely been implicated in Patna High Court CR. MISC. No.28893 of 2022(3) dt.21-11-2022 this case. It is submitted that alleged occurrence took place on 03.10.2021 and FIR for the same has been lodged on 21.10.2021 after lapse of more than 15 days.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel appearing for the petitioners submits that petitioners are innocent and have falsely been implicated in Patna High Court CR. MISC. No.28893 of 2022(3) dt.21-11-2022 this case. It is submitted that alleged occurrence took place on 03.10.2021 and FIR for the same has been lodged on 21.10.2021 after lapse of more than 15 days.",
